{"type":"npc","name":"Crystal Chimling","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":27,"temp":0,"max":27,"details":"harmonic resonance"},"ac":{"value":17,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":10,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":25}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["melodian","petran","common"],"details":"can't speak"},"level":{"value":2},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Hanging between stalactites, reclusive spider-like crystal chimlings dance in the cave breeze. Their chime song brings good fortune to their allies, heals cracks in their crystalline bodies, and wards off their enemies with painful frequencies. Crystal chimlings are drawn to pleasant and concordant melodies, including the music of other chimlings. However, discordant sounds entice chimlings to a fight or flight response. They either flee, emit an ear-splitting toll, or whip the aggravator with their crystalline tails. As a result, when crystal chimlings attack other creatures, it's usually due to misunderstandings about the nature of these painful noises. Crystal chimlings have difficulty understanding that other creatures are producing harmful sounds by accident, rather than as a premeditated attack.</p><p>Cultures that live near a chimling cave sometimes bury their dead near the cave mouth so the chimling's music can give the departed good luck in the afterlife. But not all creatures treat crystal chimling with such reverence. Unscrupulous nobles, merchants, and others who traffic with the elite pay handsomely for hunters to slay chimlings so they can use their crystals in wedding rings and lucky charms. This can devastate crystal chimling communities. If the hunting doesn't wipe them out entirely, this can leave the survivors cautious or even antagonistic toward other humanoids they encounter later, out of fear they might be looking to finish the job.</p><p>In their natural habitat, a crystal chimling bonds with a partner for life and never willingly leaves their side. They entwine their music together in a loving dance that lasts whole nights, during which some cultures gather outside to enjoy courtship dances of their own. If a crystal chimling should ever lose their partner, they perform a lengthy song of mourning before falling forever silent.</p><h2>Chimes in the Deep</h2><p>For travelers deep underground, a chimling colony can be both a safe haven and a landmark. Their communities offer healing and safety to peaceful travelers, making a chimling nest an ideal stopover point on a long journey. Furthermore, chimling music carries well through subterranean silence and stillness, helping to orient allies and beckon them toward safety. However, sound carries unpredictably underground; sometimes a freak of cavern acoustics masks the true source of chimling chimes, leading weary travelers into danger instead of toward the safety of the chimling community.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 5/12/22 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Nature, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, earth, earth armor, energy resistant (vitality), life, lifeward armor, music, throwing, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Jake Cassar","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":3},"con":{"mod":1},"int":{"mod":1},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":11,"senses":[{"type":"echolocation","acuity":"precise","range":120}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":5,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":7,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":11,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":7},"athletics":{"base":6},"nature":{"base":7},"performance":{"base":8}},"traits":{"value":["earth","elemental"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"2LKpIw7ELV0TAW1i","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/crystal-chimling.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Crystal Chimling","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/crystal-chimling.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1.6,"scaleY":1.6,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/crystal-chimling.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Echolocation","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>A crystal chimling can use their hearing as a precise sense at the listed range.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"dNOE3hJ8VXcl7qUg","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Crystal Chimes","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>A crystal chimling ordinarily has four chimes. A creature can attempt to sever one of the chimling's chimes by specifically targeting it and dealing damage equal to the chime's Hit Points. A chime that is not completely severed returns to full Hit Points at the end of any creature's turn.</p><p>Each chime has 5 HP and is immune to area damage.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"eOgV3fC8kpcrQIuD","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Harmonic Resonance","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The crystal chimling has regeneration equal to the number of chimes they have, which can't be overcome except by severing the chimes. They can replace a severed chime by finding and bonding with a suitable crystal in a process that takes 1 week.</p><p>@UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.effects.Item.t7Ueni1IWXiR19fL]{Effect: Chimes}</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["auditory","healing","primal","vitality"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"PU3u2NJQgJe4fkkJ","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Lucky Charm","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally within 30 feet of the chimling fails or critically fails a saving throw</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The crystal chimling's chimes ring for luck. The ally rerolls the saving throw and uses the better result.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["auditory","fortune","primal"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"q1PL3fmHQ82dedIf","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Sonorous Echo","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Anot